Tolerate a missing systemd in qvm-features-request is_active().

is_active() shells out to "systemctl is-active" to decide whether to advertise
the qrexec-agent feature.  On a systemd-less VM (for example a native Guix
template using the Shepherd) systemctl is absent and the call raises
FileNotFoundError, aborting feature advertisement.  Catch that and fall back to
treating the qrexec agent as active, since a running qvm-features-request itself
proves the qrexec path works.  systemd distributions are unaffected: systemctl
is present, so the original call runs unchanged.

Upstream: QubesOS/qubes-core-agent-linux, misc/qvm-features-request.
Status: should-upstream (portable; only adds a fallback for systemd-less VMs).

diff --git a/misc/qvm-features-request b/misc/qvm-features-request
index 6eccea6..7918451 100755
--- a/misc/qvm-features-request
+++ b/misc/qvm-features-request
@@ -31,7 +31,10 @@ import qubesdb
 
 
 def is_active(service):
-    status = subprocess.call(["systemctl", "is-active", "--quiet", service])
+    try:
+        status = subprocess.call(["systemctl", "is-active", "--quiet", service])
+    except FileNotFoundError:
+        return service == "qubes-qrexec-agent"
     return status == 0
 
 
